   "text": "This structure is methicillin, a penicillin with a 2,6-dimethoxybenzamide side chain. I read it region by region.\n\n- **Side chain:** a benzene ring carries two OMe groups ortho to the carbon that bears the C(=O)NH group, so it is a 2,6-dimethoxybenzoyl amide.\n- **\u03b2-lactam ring:** the amide nitrogen attaches to a ring carbon through a hashed bond. That carbon is bonded to the lactam C=O, which is bonded to the ring N. The ring N is bonded to the ring-fusion carbon, which carries an H on a wedge.\n- **Thiazolidine ring:** the ring N is bonded to a carbon that carries the COOH on a wedge. That carbon is bonded to C(CH3)2, which is bonded to S, and S is bonded back to the ring-fusion carbon.\n- **Stereocentres:** I assigned the three stereocentres (the amide-bearing carbon, the COOH-bearing carbon and the ring-fusion carbon) from the wedge and hash bonds. In the SMILES they are the first, second and third `@@`/`@` centres, written `[C@@H]`, `[C@@H]` and `[C@H]`.\n\nSMILES: COc1cccc(OC)c1C(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N2[C@@H](C(=O)O)C(C)(C)S[C@H]12"
